<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bay of Biscay</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bay of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/biscay">Biscay</a> is the gulf of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-ocean">Atlantic Ocean</a> bounded by the west coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and the north coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, from Brittany to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a>. Known for storms and heavy swells, it was an important fishing and whaling ground for Basque and Breton sailors. The Cantabrian coast along its southern shore was home to the Callaeci, Astures, Cantabri and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basques">Basques</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bay-of-biscay.jpg" alt="Bay of Biscay" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Iago Casabiell González · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Praia_de_Bares_4IX2015.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
